# Table 2 under every equidistant period length

Sample: the 487 OMXSB events of `events_car.csv` (2007–2026), period = calendar year of the effective date. Lengths are the divisors of the 20-year window so every period has the same length; 2026 contains only the June review. Cells: mean CAR in percent against .OMXSBGI, stars from the HC1 p-value, HC1 SE in parentheses, SE clustered on announcement date in brackets, wild cluster bootstrap p in braces, N. F = cluster-robust F for equal means across the periods (p from F(k−1, G−1)). Trend = OLS of the CAR on the period index, slope per period and per year, CR1 SE, p from t(G−1) and the wild bootstrap. For one period the F-test and the trend do not exist; with one-year periods three periods (2007, 2010, 2026) contain a single announcement date, so their clustered SE and bootstrap p are n/a and the F-test is singular.

